				31,
				0
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add Apple platform support assets and Xcode project configuration\nchore(SideCar): Remove .DS_Store files from runtime directories\n\nThis commit introduces two architectural improvements:\n\n1. **Mountain** now includes comprehensive Apple platform support (commit 9afa88da). The changes add:\n   - Asset catalog with AppIcons (20x20 to 1024x1024) compliant with Apple HIG\n   - Xcode project with Metal framework integration and ARM64/x86_64 support\n   - Podfile setup for iOS/macOS targets\n   - LaunchScreen storyboard and entitlements\n   - Submodule inclusion of macOS/Mountain (commit 5c5b7c0)\n   This enables Land's cross-platform expansion through Tauri's iOS target while maintaining separation between Mountain's native backend and Wind/Sky's UI layer.\n\n2. **SideCar** removes accidental .DS_Store files (commit 592c76e7) from architecture-specific runtime directories (aarch64-apple-darwin, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, etc.). These macOS Finder metadata files were unnecessary for the pre-compiled Node.js runtimes stored in SideCar, and their removal improves repository hygiene without affecting runtime behavior.\n\nBoth changes align with Land's architectural principles of resource efficiency and strict separation between native backend components (Mountain) and runtime dependencies (SideCar).",
			"SHA": "c8f303c2b4f14cc868969a1c8a5f45cb20ebb94d"
		},
